        "calls": 3,
        "title": "CLI distinguishes refund and closed hour errors from session takeovers",
        "summary": "The Freebuff CLI now parses the server message attached to a session superseded error to determine if the session was refunded, closed at the end of the hour, or taken over by another instance. For refunded starts and closed hours, the session is ended locally and the user is shown the server message, with a hint to retry or switch models appended to refund errors. Takeover errors retain the previous behavior of marking the session as superseded. This prevents the CLI from incorrectly prompting a restart when the user simply needs to retry the request on a different model.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/utils/error-handling.ts`, the new `getFreebuffSupersededReason` function classifies server messages for session superseded errors into 'refunded_start', 'session_closed', or 'taken_over'. In `cli/src/hooks/helpers/send-message.ts`, the `handleFreebuffGateError` function now uses this classification to end the session for refunds or closed hours, appending `FREEBUFF_REFUNDED_START_HINT` to the error message.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "at": "2026-10-07T00:08:57.983Z",
        "cf": "90122e372b5d"
